---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About Taieui Song" description="Meet Taieui Song, the AI engineer behind teimakes: notes on LLMs, attention, RAG, agents, and AI-assisted creative work.">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>About Taieui Song</h1>
    <p>AI engineering, research, and creative experiments.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>I'm Taieui Song, an AI engineer interested in large language models and AI-assisted filmmaking, animation, and manga. I publish my technical notes and experiments here as teimakes.</p>
    <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/posts/attention-01-big-picture-ko/">Attention and Transformers</a>: explanations and PyTorch learning exercises.</li>
      <li><a href="/posts/full-context-vs-rag-ko/">LLM systems and RAG</a>: experiments, evaluation, and implementation tradeoffs.</li>
      <li><a href="/posts/building-my-first-ai-agent/">AI agents</a>: tools and workflows.</li>
      <li><a href="/posts/ai-animation-tools-2025/">Creative AI</a>: tools for animation and visual storytelling.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Research, code, and contact</h2>
    <p>Find my research profile on <a href={SITE.social['Google Scholar']} rel="me">Google Scholar</a>, code on <a href={SITE.social.GitHub} rel="me">GitHub</a>, and professional profile on <a href={SITE.social.LinkedIn} rel="me">LinkedIn</a>. You can contact me through LinkedIn or report a correction in <a href="https://github.com/teimakes/teimakes.github.io/issues">the blog's GitHub issues</a>. Please keep private information out of public issues.</p>
    <p>These are personal notes. Results depend on the models, data, and settings described in each post. Use the linked sources and experiment details when assessing or reproducing them.</p>
    <p>Some articles are available in both Korean and English; a language link appears when a translation exists. Follow new posts with <a href="/subscribe/">RSS or JSON Feed</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
